" (https://electionresults.sos.mn.gov/Results/MediaFileLayout/Index?erselectionId=201)\nciteturn34view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: text/plain; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn33view0\",\"id\":13}); Total lines: 203\nL0: Office of the Minnesota Secretary of State (OSS)\nL1: \nL2: 2026 State General Election Results\nL3: ----------------------------------------------------\nL4: \nL5:  - The filenames given below are part of the URLs on the Election Night Reporting website and used on the ftp site.\nL6:  - The files on OSS web and ftp sites contain ASCII text, separated by semicolons.\nL7:  - Information in the supporting files is subject to correction and change up until election day.\nL8:  - Election results may change after being reported initially on election night.\nL9:  - Files with precinct-level results will not be available until the morning after election day.\nL10:  - For questions, contact OSS Elections Division at elections.dept@state.mn.us\nL11: \nL12: Last revised 06/03/2026\nL13: \nL14: ----------------------------------------------------\nL15: Election Results Files\nL16: ----------------------------------------------------\nL17: Results are formatted in flat files which have one row for each candidate and question response in each geographic area\nL18: (statewide, county, district, or precinct, depending on the file).\nL19: \nL20: Election Results (various names)\nL21: \nL22: \tState\nL23: \tCounty ID (if applicable)\nL24: \tPrecinct name (if applicable)\nL25: \tOffice ID\nL26: \tOffice Name\nL27: \tDistrict*\nL28: \tCandidate Order Code**\nL29: \tCandidate Name (First/Last/Suffix all in one field)\nL30: \tSuffix (not used)\nL31: \tIncumbent Code (not used)\nL32: \tParty Abbreviation***\nL33: \tNumber of Precincts reporting\nL34: \tTotal number of precincts voting for the office\nL35: \tVotes for Candidate\nL36: \tPercentage of Votes for Candidate out of Total Votes for Office\nL37: \tTotal number of votes for Office in area\nL38: *Note: The District field is used for U.S. Representative, State Senate, State Representative, and County Commissioner districts; District Court; school district numbers; municipal FIPS codes; soil and water conservation district codes, and hospital district codes. The District field is not used for statewide offices (U.S. President, U.S. Senate, Governor, Secretary of State, State Auditor, Attorney General, Supreme Court, Court of Appeals), county-wide offices, or city wards.\nL39: **Note: Code for write-in candidates is 9901\nL40: ***Note: All local candidates are non-partisan.\nL41: \nL42: ----------------------------------------------------\nL43: \nL44: Precinct Voting Statistics (pctstats.txt)\nL45: \nL46:         State\nL47:         County ID\nL48:         Precinct ID\nL49:         Precinct Name\nL50:         Has Reported Statistics (1 = yes, 0 = no)\nL51:         Number of Voters Registered as of 7:00 a.m. Election Day\nL52:         Number of Voters that Registered on Election Day\nL53:         Number of Signatures on the Polling Place Roster\nL54:         Number of Regular, Military, and Overseas Absentee Ballots\nL55:         Number of Federal-Only Absentee Ballots\nL56:         Number of President-Only Absentee Ballots\nL57:         Total Number Voted\nL58: \nL59: ----------------------------------------------------\nL60: Supporting Tables for Election\nL61: ----------------------------------------------------\nL62: \nL63: Parties (PartyTbl.txt)\nL64: \nL65: \tParty Abbreviation\nL66: \tParty Name\nL67: \tParty ID\nL68: \nL69: Note: all local candidates are non-partisan.\nL70: ----------------------------------------------------\nL71: \nL72: Counties (CntyTbl.txt)\nL73: \nL74: \tCounty ID\nL75: \tCounty Name\nL76: \tNumber of precincts\nL77: \nL78: ----------------------------------------------------\nL79: \nL80: Precincts (PrctTbl.txt)\nL81: \nL82: \tCounty ID\nL83: \tPrecinct ID\nL84: \tPrecinct Name\nL85: \tCongressional District\nL86: \tLegislative District\nL87: \tCounty Commissioner District\nL88: \tJudicial District\nL89: \tSoil and Water Conservation District\nL90: \tMCD FIPS code*\nL91: \tSchool District number (not used in statewide elections)\nL92: * FIPS codes for precincts in unorganized territories may vary from Census FIPS codes.\nL93: \nL94: ----------------------------------------------------\nL95: \nL96: Federal, State, and County Candidates (cand.txt)\nL97: \nL98: \tCandidate ID (eight characters)\nL99: \tCandidate Name (First/Last/Suffix all in one field)\nL100: \tOffice ID\nL101: \tOffice Title\nL102: \tCounty ID (88 = statewide race or multi-county race)\nL103: \tParty ID\nL104: \tParty Abbreviation\nL105: \nL106: ----------------------------------------------------\nL107: Federal, State, and County Candidates with Contact Information (CandTbl.txt)\nL108: \nL109: \tCandidate ID (eight characters)\nL110: \tCandidate Name (First/Last/Suffix all in one field)\nL111: \tOffice ID\nL112: \tOffice Title\nL113: \tCounty ID (88 = statewide or multi-county race)\nL114: \tParty ID\nL115: \tParty Abbreviation\nL116: \tResidence Street Address\nL117: \tResidence City\nL118: \tResidence State\nL119: \tResidence Zip\nL120: \tCampaign Address\nL121: \tCampaign City\nL122: \tCampaign State\nL123: \tCampaign Zip\nL124: \tCampaign Phone\nL125: \tCampaign Website\nL126: \tCampaign Email\nL127: \tRunning Mate Website\nL128: \tRunning Mate Email\nL129: \tRunning Mate Phone\nL130: \nL131: Note: Semicolons in address fields have been replaced with the caret (^) character\nL132: \nL133: ----------------------------------------------------\nL134: \nL135: Municipal, School, and Hospital District Candidates (LocalCandTbl.txt)\nL136: \nL137: \tCandidate ID (thirteen characters)\nL138: \tCandidate Name (First/Last/Suffix all in one field)\nL139: \tOffice ID\nL140: \tOffice Title\nL141: \tCounty ID (home county if multi-county race)\nL142: \tMCD FIPS Code (if applicable)\nL143: \tSchool District Number (if applicable)\nL